<title>JAPAN: Japan to act properly on wild forex moves -- MOF.</title>
<headline>Japan to act properly on wild forex moves -- MOF.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan will continue to act appropriately towards excessive movements in the currency market, but is now watching market movements calmly, Finance Minister Hiroshi Mitsuzuka said on Monday.  </p>
<p>He said he could not specify the reasons for the recent plunge in stock prices.</p>
<p>&quot;I think the markets will stabilise if we tackle various deregulation measures with full force,&quot; Mitsuzuka said.</p>
</text>
